WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Um

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.920
I'm I'm planning a keynote for SM Bash

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.760
and it's about the role of a CEO and

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:11.280
I've got two quotes for you and I wanted

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:13.080
I want to know where you stand. So, one

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:17.040
is Andrew Wilkinson and this is his

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:18.840
tweet from 2020, March 2020.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.960
He says, "As a CEO, your job is to

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.200
actually do nothing. CEOs who perform

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.680
duties within their companies are

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.040
failing. Your job is to set strategy and

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.880
culture, delegate and incentivize. Same

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.480
goes for executives. You are just more

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.960
more focused mini CEOs who report up."

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.920
So, that's Andrew Wilkinson.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.280
And then you got Michael Gerli who says,

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.960
"Hire smart people, leave them alone.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.000
Terrible advice."

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.960
Where do you stand? Two smart people,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.760
opposite advice.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.840
>> Yeah, um both of them more successful

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.240
than me, probably, but in my opinion, to

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.400
be an effective manager, you have to be

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.880
able to get in a meeting and tell people

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.160
what to do. You can't do that if you

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.360
don't know what it's like on the front

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.320
on the front

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.480
row.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:59.680
So, in somewhere like I know how to

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.360
recruit. I know how to recruit almost

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.480
any pe- person. I know how to get it in

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.400
our software. I know how to look at

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.560
their profiles. I know how to move them

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.360
along in our sourcing. I know how to

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.720
request a video because I wrote the

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.880
email that we send

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.080
to a candidate to request a video.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.760
I wrote all the templates that my

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.360
recruiters are using to to present

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.120
candidates to clients.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:22.640
I am in I Yesterday at 4:30, I got on

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:24.800
and coached for an hour our sales team

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:26.800
because I took 20 sales calls over the

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.770
last month.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.120
So,

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:31.800
>> [laughter]

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.800
>> um that's what that's where I stand.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:37.120
>> Yeah, I like to say is like a CEO should

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.320
know what all the weeds are, but not

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.000
spend his day in the weeds. You know,

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.400
but I think most CEOs don't even know

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.440
what the weeds are. They're too far

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.000
removed from it. And they're like,

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:47.240
"Well, I'm the CEO, right?"

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.560
>> You really have to

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.240
it's my job and then it's our job and

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.200
then it's your job. People delegate too

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.040
fast. A lot of CEOs delegate too fast

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.240
and COOs. Meaning, a problem comes in,

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.640
they know the solution, they're just

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.200
going to send a quick message, no

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:01.720
meeting necessary, no meetings at my

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.960
company. I'm just going to tell somebody

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.880
quickly what to do, no follow-up, no

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.000
holding them accountable, no walking

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.119
them through it, no watching them.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.320
Um

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:12.200
yeah, for

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.240
for a couple months

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.880
my head of ops at somewhere was CC'd on

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.160
every recruiting email.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:18.160
Because you can't see what's happening.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:21.200
You don't know what's happening unless

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.160
you're really in the trenches.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.720
>> Yeah.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.640
Yeah, I told one of the things I told my

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.680
CEO, this was a shop five minutes and I

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.280
said, "I want you to turn on

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.080
notifications for all of our orders."

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.959
And he's like, "What? Like, that would

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.840
blow my phone up." I'm like, "You need

00:02:32.959 --> 00:02:36.560
to see. Like, you just need to see. You

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.240
need to stay top of mind on the size of

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.880
the orders, the name of the person

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:41.200
ordering." Cuz it was it was e-commerce,

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.480
but it was B2B, so there were bigger

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.000
orders. And you just need to have your

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.760
finger on the pulse of it. And in that

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.720
business with that method, it was just a

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:51.240
good way of doing that. So.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.640
>> That's what AI AI is overblown in my

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.560
opinion, but there's one thing it's

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.360
really good at, it's quality control.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.200
And I can get an AI notification in my

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:01.239
Slack channel every time a client sends

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:03.040
my recruiter negative feedback.

00:03:01.239 --> 00:03:05.040
And me, as the owner of the business,

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.200
can see and read where my company's

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.920
getting negative feedback.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.200
Critical. Critical, critical. If I was

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.640
just ignoring that, burying my head in

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.959
the sand,

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:15.480
I wouldn't know what to do to improve

